# JANET configuration — copy to `.env` and fill in what you use.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# `.env` is gitignored: it holds real passwords and tokens, so it must never be
# committed. Everything here is OPTIONAL — JANET's core (listening, transcribing,
# intents, timers, alarms, maths, the local LLM) needs none of it. These keys only
# switch on the integrations that reach outside the machine.
#
# Every integration also has a "demo" backend: a fake, in-memory version with
# believable sample data. Set the `=demo` keys below to try JANET's calendar,
# weather, smart-home and email out with no accounts, no servers, no credentials.
# That's also how the automated checks run.


# ─── The language model (JANET's voice) ──────────────────────────────────────
# JANET speaks through an LLM: handlers produce facts, the model turns them into
# what you actually hear. It talks over the OpenAI-compatible /v1 HTTP API, so
# the backend is just a URL and there's no client library to install.
#
# Default is a llama.cpp server, which is worth knowing about: if you run
# llama-server with the model fully on the GPU (-ngl 999), JANET reuses those
# loaded weights. Running Ollama alongside it loads a SECOND copy into whatever
# VRAM is left, which pushes it onto the CPU and makes every reply 3-5x slower.
#
#JANET_LLM_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8081/v1      # llama.cpp (default)
#JANET_LLM_URL=http://127.0.0.1:11434/v1     # Ollama instead
#JANET_LLM_MODEL=qwen3-14b                   # ignored by single-model llama.cpp

# Let JANET escalate itself to full step-by-step thinking on hard questions.
# It says something casual first ("hang on, let me think about that one") so the
# pause isn't dead air. OFF by default: it takes ~11-20s and JANET is
# single-threaded, so the mic is deaf for that whole window.
#JANET_DEEP_THINKING=1


# ─── Calendar ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Pick ONE: demo, google, or CalDAV (leave JANET_CALENDAR unset for CalDAV).

# The fake calendar — sample events seeded around "now". No server needed.
#JANET_CALENDAR=demo

# CalDAV. Point this at a self-hosted Radicale/Nextcloud and it stays fully local.
# All three keys are required or JANET reports the calendar as not set up.
#JANET_CALDAV_URL=https://example.com/dav/
#JANET_CALDAV_USER=you
#JANET_CALDAV_PASSWORD=app-specific-password

# Google Calendar. One-time setup:
#   1. Google Cloud console -> new project -> enable the Google Calendar API
#   2. OAuth consent screen -> External -> add yourself as a test user
#   3. Credentials -> OAuth client ID -> Desktop app -> download the JSON
#   4. Save it to the path below, then run the consent ONCE from a terminal
#      (never mid-conversation — it opens a browser and would block the mic):
#         cd src && ../venv/bin/python -c \
#           "from integrations.google_calendar_source import authorize; authorize()"
#JANET_CALENDAR=google
#JANET_GOOGLE_CREDENTIALS=~/.config/janet/google_credentials.json
#JANET_GOOGLE_TOKEN=~/.config/janet/google_token.json


# ─── Weather ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Uses Open-Meteo, which needs NO API key. Give it either a city (geocoded for
# you) or explicit coordinates. Temperatures are Celsius.

#JANET_WEATHER=demo
#JANET_WEATHER_CITY=Pune
#JANET_WEATHER_LAT=18.5196
#JANET_WEATHER_LON=73.8553


# ─── Smart home (Home Assistant) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Home Assistant on your own LAN, so this stays local. The token is a
# long-lived access token from your HA profile page.
# Only lights, switches and fans are controllable — locks, garage doors and
# alarm panels are deliberately excluded and cannot be voice-controlled.

#JANET_SMART_HOME=demo
#JANET_HA_URL=http://homeassistant.local:8123
#JANET_HA_TOKEN=your-long-lived-access-token


# ─── Email ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Reading is IMAP and uses BODY.PEEK, so JANET checking your mail never marks
# it as read. Gmail/Outlook need an APP-SPECIFIC password, not your login one.

#JANET_EMAIL=demo
#JANET_IMAP_HOST=imap.gmail.com
#JANET_IMAP_USER=you@example.com
#JANET_IMAP_PASSWORD=app-specific-password
#JANET_IMAP_PORT=993

# Sending is only used to REPLY to the message you just heard about, and always
# asks for a spoken confirmation first. Leave these unset to keep JANET
# read-only; it will say "Sending isn't set up yet."
#JANET_SMTP_HOST=smtp.gmail.com
#JANET_SMTP_PORT=465
#JANET_SMTP_USER=you@example.com
#JANET_SMTP_PASSWORD=app-specific-password
#JANET_EMAIL_FROM=you@example.com
